# Platform Tests, Evidence, and Report Format

## Android

APK must be built, installed, launched, and actually tested. Verify: app name AveroNova, icon AN, startup, splash, create account, login, offline, online, offline → online. No startup crash. Install-but-crash = Android E2E FAIL.

## Windows

Verify the actual Windows app: launch → branding → auth → SQLite → offline → online → sync. Build success alone is not enough.

## BrowserStack

Always verify the APK under test is the NEW APK. Report filename, size, and path/build identifier. Never claim a new fix passed on an old APK.

If BrowserStack cannot reach the local Development API: report **ENVIRONMENT LIMITATION**. Do not report PASS. Use a real Android device on the same development network for local API E2E when appropriate.

## Evidence required for every final PASS

```
Test: <name>
Environment: <Windows/Android/etc.>
Input: <what was done>
Expected: <expected result>
Actual: <actual result>
Database verification: PASS/FAIL
API verification: PASS/FAIL
Runtime verification: PASS/FAIL
E2E: PASS/FAIL
```

## Mandatory feature report

```
FEATURE: <name>
IMPLEMENTATION: PASS/FAIL
BUILD: PASS/FAIL
RUNTIME: PASS/FAIL
DATABASE: PASS/FAIL/NOT APPLICABLE
API: PASS/FAIL/NOT APPLICABLE
OFFLINE: PASS/FAIL/NOT APPLICABLE
ONLINE: PASS/FAIL/NOT APPLICABLE
SYNC: PASS/FAIL/NOT APPLICABLE
E2E: PASS/FAIL/NOT VERIFIED
REGRESSION: PASS/FAIL/NOT VERIFIED
KNOWN LIMITATIONS: <list>
ROOT CAUSE OF ANY FAILURE: <actual cause>
FINAL STATUS: DONE / FAILED / NOT VERIFIED
```

Use only those final statuses. DONE only when complete E2E acceptance criteria PASS.
